ility was extracted and introduced to SVM for slide-based scores. For ATSA and RNNSA, the original papers used Multi instance learning (MIL) for patch-wise training, whereas we considered pretrained models of CAT-Net and GB. For all methods, the hyper-parameters of the learning rate and L2-norm regularization were obtained to optimize the validation data using a grid search 51 . HipoMap was implemented in Keras with TensorFlow as back-end. The performances of HipoMap with various top-patch size K were evaluated (Table 2 ). A lower value of the hyperparameter K may cause missing some important patches to conduct the slide-based analysis, whereas a higher value of K may include more false positive patches in the representation map. We used K =50, which showed the best performance on the validation, for all experiments in this paper. For the comparison, we considered two pretrained CNN models with patches of size 299 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
